    "c1": {
      "anchor": "p-spell-ui-site#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Spell UI Site",
      "excerpt": "Owen, 2026-11-08: \"I'd like to move this over to a 'site' like the mockup epic h",
      "text": "This should be in guides, not examples",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-08T17:44:30.363Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "spell/examples/SpellUISite",
      "offset": 259,
      "edited": "2026-11-08T17:44:37.191Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-08T18:41:02.831Z",
          "html": "<p>Done in the plan: the project is now <code>@spell/guides/SpellUI</code>, and every address follows it, tests included. <code>@spell/examples/SpellUISite</code> and its snapshots go; nothing replaces them, since a site of imported pages is no longer anything Spell does. It stays off the Guides row of the home page through a new project setting, <code>onHome: false</code> (the Guides group otherwise adds only a Guide type and a create button; a guide's tests are the example's snapshots, and it's left out of those too).</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-08T18:40:25.790Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "p-spell-ui-site#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Spell UI Site",
      "excerpt": "Owen, 2026-11-08: \"I'd like to move this over to a 'site' like the mockup epic h",
      "text": "We're going to want something like this, but I agree that it shouldn't be a separate page.  Maybe this is a subset of table of contents?  Or a new widget.  This is a general pattern that we are going to want to have.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-08T17:45:17.526Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "93 tab bar files and the",
      "offset": 980,
      "edited": "2026-11-08T17:46:43.594Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-08T18:41:04.443Z",
          "html": "<p>Done in the plan (<a href=\"#q10\">Q10</a>): a new element, <code>&lt;ui-site-tabs&gt;</code>, beside <code>&lt;ui-site-nav&gt;</code> and reading the same page tree. The site draws it by itself above any page with sub-pages, or one that is one: parent first, the shown page selected, real links, the segmented look the tab bars have, one row on a phone, English and Spanish, a docs page and examples. A parent page can say what its tab is called (<code>tab=\"Usage\"</code>), since the side navigation calls it Button; the tab bars and their lines still go.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-08T18:40:26.824Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "p-spell-ui-site#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Spell UI Site",
      "excerpt": "Owen, 2026-11-08: \"I'd like to move this over to a 'site' like the mockup epic h",
      "text": "add to this phase",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-08T17:48:24.667Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Rejected for this phase: the listing, the drafts, the file list and the source maps would all have to learn sub-folders, and flat names read better in the file list anyway.",
      "offset": 5215,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-08T18:41:06.568Z",
          "html": "<p>Done in the plan: sub-folders are this phase's first step, each component a folder (<code>Button/Usage.spellml</code>). The census, in the Goal: 10 readers already cope with a folder (addresses, saving, drafts, source maps ...), 8 must learn it (<code>getIndex()</code>, the file list, error messages, the language server's scope list, <code>&lt;spell-editor&gt;</code>'s <code>file</code>, renaming and deleting, and two test loops). The project file still names each file, <code>\"/Button/Usage.spellml\"</code>, as it names every file today.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-08T18:40:27.786Z"
      }
    },
    "c4": {
      "anchor": "p-spell-ui-site#field-4",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Spell UI Site",
      "excerpt": "Move the files. One TypeScript codemod, run once and not kept (the repo's rule:",
      "text": "It would be fine to say that `<spell-page>` is the only thing in its file, and that it should not have anything that gets exported to other pages.  So pages can be compiled independently, and the app can be compiled without the pages.  Maybe?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-08T17:49:19.015Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Make typing fast again",
      "offset": 2261,
      "edited": "2026-11-08T17:50:26.162Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-08T18:41:08.792Z",
          "html": "<p>Done in the plan (<a href=\"#q11\">Q11</a>), and checked against the compiler first, in a scratch copy: a page alone in its file parses in its own small scope and is written by itself; the code came out byte-identical to today's for 351 of 351 pages. A keystroke in Button's Examples is about 83 ms (56 parse, 27 write) against 5-7 s and 2.4 s. A file that isn't one page alone compiles as today, with no error. A view inside a page is now that page's own, reversing <a href=\"#q7\">Q7</a>: it's named for the page, and two pages can each have one. Nothing used one from another file (checked).</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-08T18:40:29.084Z"
      }
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
